meta {
  name: 04 Discover inputs (smart walker — empty body)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/v1/factgraph/{{ruleset_id}}/query
  body: json
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "targets": ["/eligible"]
  }
}

docs {
  Send a query with nothing but a target. The server runs the engine
  with empty inputs, walks the dependency graph, propagates "still
  needed" back through any unprovided collections, and returns the
  full set of writables required to determine `/eligible`.

  Expect `status: "incomplete"`, `values: { "/eligible": null }`, and
  `missingInputs` listing all required writables: 11 scalars + 18
  per-member fields.

  This is the call a partner UI makes on first load to render an empty
  intake form. As the user fills in fields and the UI re-POSTs with
  the partial values, `missingInputs` shrinks (see request 05).
}
